@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam participantPadding 20
skinparam boxPadding 10

title Plum Claims Processing — LLM-Driven Orchestrator

actor "Member" as MEMBER
actor "Ops Team" as OPS

box "Frontend" #E8F4FD
  participant "Streamlit UI" as UI
end box

box "Backend API" #F0E6FF
  participant "FastAPI\n(POST /api/claims)" as API
  participant "Pipeline\n(Orchestrator Agent)" as PIPE
end box

box "Sub-Agents (called as tools)" #E8FFE8
  participant "DocVerifierAgent" as A1
  participant "DocExtractorAgent\n(vision)" as A2
  participant "PolicyCheckerAgent" as A3
  participant "FraudDetectorAgent" as A4
  participant "DecisionMakerAgent" as A5
end box

box "Infrastructure" #FFF3E0
  database "PostgreSQL" as DB
  entity "Groq API\n(llama-3.3-70b / llama-4-scout)" as GROQ
end box

== 1. Claim Submission ==
MEMBER -> UI: Upload docs + fill form
UI -> API: POST /api/claims [SSE stream]
API -> DB: INSERT claim (status=PROCESSING)
API --> UI: SSE: { claim_id, status: PROCESSING }

== 2. Orchestrator Agent (LLM decides workflow) ==
API -> PIPE: run_pipeline(claim_data, policy_terms, api_key)
note right #F0E6FF
  Orchestrator has 5 tools.
  System prompt tells it the
  workflow rules. LLM decides
  which tool to call next and
  in what order.
end note

PIPE -> GROQ: [system prompt + user claim data + tools]
GROQ --> PIPE: tool_call: verify_documents(...)

|||
||| Orchestrator loop: LLM decides → execute tool → feed back → LLM decides again |||
|||

PIPE -> A1: verify_documents (called as tool)
A1 -> A1: Classify docs, validate set
A1 --> PIPE: { valid, classified_docs, error_message }

alt Verification failed
  PIPE --> API: SSE: error + done
  note right #FFB3B3: Early exit — no more tool calls
  API --> UI: Show specific error
else Passed
  PIPE -> GROQ: result fed back → LLM decides next
  GROQ --> PIPE: tool_call: extract_documents(...)
end

PIPE -> A2: extract_documents (vision tool)
A2 -> GROQ: Vision API with base64 images
GROQ --> A2: { extracted_data, overall_confidence, status }
A2 --> PIPE: result

PIPE -> GROQ: result fed back → LLM decides next
GROQ --> PIPE: tool_call: check_policy(...)
note right #F0E6FF
  LLM may call check_policy
  and detect_fraud in either
  order or even parallel
end note

PIPE -> A3: check_policy (tool)
A3 -> GROQ: Policy rules evaluation
A3 --> PIPE: { all_passed, approved_amount, copay_amount, policy_checks }

PIPE -> GROQ: result fed back → LLM decides next
GROQ --> PIPE: tool_call: detect_fraud(...)

PIPE -> A4: detect_fraud (tool)
A4 -> DB: Query claims history
A4 -> GROQ: Fraud analysis
A4 --> PIPE: { fraud_score, fraud_flags, recommendation }

PIPE -> GROQ: result fed back → LLM decides next
GROQ --> PIPE: tool_call: decide_claim(...)

PIPE -> A5: decide_claim (tool - final)
A5 -> GROQ: Synthesise all results → final decision
GROQ --> A5: { decision, approved_amount, reason, confidence, trace }
A5 --> PIPE: Final decision with full trace

== 3. Result ==
PIPE -> DB: UPDATE Claim + INSERT DecisionRecord
PIPE --> API: SSE: { result } → { done }
API --> UI: Show decision, amount, reason, trace

alt MANUAL_REVIEW
  UI --> OPS: Notify team
  OPS -> UI: Review trace, approve/override
end

== 4. Trace / Explainability ==
OPS -> API: GET /api/claims/{id}
API -> DB: SELECT claim + trace
API --> OPS: Full decision + agent outputs

@enduml
